      image: 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1434626881859-194d67b2b86f?w=1200&h=630&fit=crop&auto=format&q=80',
      excerpt: "Hiring a Philippine studio for offshore web design in Australia works well. Here's how time zones, payment and project handover actually run.",
      content: `
        <p>Offshore web design from Australia — working with a studio in the Philippines — is practical when you know how the project runs. Most of the Australian business day overlaps with Manila working hours, the build runs on written briefs and staging links, and a good studio can deliver a complete website in seven business days. Here is what to expect.</p>
        <h2>Why offshore web design in Australia is worth considering</h2>
        <p>The main reason Australian businesses hire a Philippine studio is value for money. Fixed-price packages differ from studio to studio; ours are $499 (Starter), $899 (Growth) and $1,499 (Pro), all launched in seven business days. The AUD amount you pay depends on the exchange rate on the day of payment, but the difference between a Philippine studio and a local Australian agency is generally significant. You get a professionally built site, owned outright, with no lock-in contract.</p>
        <p>Quality has also changed. The tools, frameworks and web standards a good Manila studio uses are the same ones an Australian developer would use. When you check a studio's portfolio, look at live URLs — not mockups. If the sites load quickly, look clean on mobile, and match the style you need, the location matters far less than the work itself.</p>
        <h2>How time zones work in your favour</h2>
        <p>Australian clients have a genuine advantage over US or UK clients when working with a Manila studio. Brisbane is two hours ahead of Manila; Sydney and Melbourne are two to three hours ahead depending on daylight saving; Perth is roughly the same time as Manila. That means most of the Australian business day overlaps with Manila working hours — 8:30am to 5:00pm Philippine time, Monday to Friday.</p>
        <p>In practice, a morning call your time puts the Manila team in their afternoon. Written feedback you send in the afternoon arrives at the start of their next day. A scheduled call for kickoff, staging review, and final walkthrough is feasible during normal business hours for both parties — something US clients cannot easily arrange.</p>
        <h2>What the build process looks like</h2>
        <p>A seven-day build follows a clear sequence. Day 1: you send a brief — your logo, images, copy for each page, brand colours, and links to two or three sites whose style you like. The studio confirms scope, you pay a 50% deposit, and work starts. During the build you receive a staging link at each milestone, leave written notes, and the studio applies changes during their working day. A final walkthrough call wraps things up before handover.</p>
        <p><strong>The most common reason projects run long is missing content.</strong> If the studio is waiting for your logo or copy, the seven-day clock does not start until the content is in their hands. Gather everything before you sign anything and the timeline holds.</p>
        <p>For a broader look at how to vet a studio and what questions to ask before you hire, our guide on <a href="https://www.fazeddigital.com/blog/outsource-web-development-philippines">outsourcing web development to the Philippines</a> covers briefs, time zones, portfolio checks, and payment in detail.</p>
        <h2>Paying a Philippine studio from Australia</h2>
        <p>Most Philippine studios accept payment by Wise or international bank transfer. Wise is the most common choice for Australian clients — transfer fees are low and the exchange rate is clear before you confirm. Standard terms are a 50% deposit before work starts, with the balance due on delivery. IP in the final deliverables passes to you on full payment, and you keep the domain, site files, and all content with no retainer required.</p>
        <p>Fazed quotes in USD only. The AUD amount depends on the exchange rate on the day of payment. On GST: the tax treatment of overseas digital services for Australian businesses depends on your circumstances and the ATO's current rules for imported services — your accountant can confirm what applies to your situation.</p>
        <h2>What you own when the project ends</h2>
        <p>Ownership is straightforward when the terms are clear upfront. You own the domain, the site files, and all the content on delivery. There is no lock-in contract and no obligation to stay on a care plan. Ask any studio you are considering to state this in writing before work begins.</p>
        <p>One example from our own work: The Telecom Shop is an Australian online retailer that needed their full catalogue, customer data, and order history moved from Magento to PrestaShop. The migration ran over ten weeks with zero data loss and minimal disruption to trading. Read the full story at the <a href="https://www.fazeddigital.com/work/04">The Telecom Shop case study</a>.</p>
        <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
        <p><strong>How do I pay a Philippine studio from Australia?</strong> The most common method is Wise, which gives you a transparent exchange rate and low transfer fees. International bank transfer also works. Most studios quote in USD; what you pay in AUD depends on the exchange rate at the time of payment.</p>
        <p><strong>What happens if the project runs over time?</strong> Ask about the studio's on-time policy before you commit. Our guarantee is 20% off the project fee if we miss the agreed launch date on our side — your content must arrive on day one and feedback must come within 24 hours at each review stage for the guarantee to apply.</p>
        <p><strong>Do I need to be available during Manila business hours?</strong> Not for most of the project. The bulk of the work runs on written updates, a staging link, and email. Scheduled calls — kickoff, review, handover — can be timed to overlap with Australian business hours, which the time difference makes easy.</p>
        <p>To see what is included in a seven-day website build, browse <a href="https://www.fazeddigital.com/lp/7-day-website">our 7-day website packages</a> — scope, prices, and how to reserve a spot for your build.</p>
      `,
