    {
      slug: 'seo-iligan-city',
      title: "SEO in Iligan City: How Local Businesses Get Found on Google",
      category: 'SEO',
      date: '20 Oct 2026',
      readTime: '4 min read',
      author: 'Russel Heyrana',
      authorRole: 'Marketing Director',
      authorPhoto: '/images/team/russel.jpeg',
      image: 'https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1461749280684-dccba630e2f6?w=1200&h=630&fit=crop&auto=format&q=80',
      excerpt: "Local SEO in Iligan City starts with basics most owners overlook. Here is what to fix — and what it takes to appear when local customers search for you.",
      content: `
        <p>SEO in Iligan City starts with your Google Business Profile and a website that clearly tells Google where you are and what you do. Local businesses that get these basics right appear when people nearby search for their service. This guide covers the practical steps — profile setup, on-page signals, and citations — that help local customers find you.</p>
        <h2>Why local SEO matters for Iligan City businesses</h2>
        <p>When someone in Iligan types "car wash near me" or "construction supply Iligan" into Google, they are ready to act — not just browse. Google's local algorithm surfaces results based on how relevant, prominent, and close a business is to the searcher. Iligan has a growing number of businesses competing for the same phrases. Without clear local signals, even an established shop can be invisible online while a newer competitor with a complete profile appears first.</p>
        <p>This is not unique to Iligan. Businesses across Northern Mindanao that invest a few hours in local SEO consistently appear above those that rely on word of mouth alone — not because they are better businesses, but because they are easier to find.</p>
        <h2>Build your Google Business Profile first</h2>
        <p>Your Google Business Profile is the most direct lever you have for local visibility. It controls what appears in Maps results and the local pack — the box of three businesses Google shows above the regular search results.</p>
        <p>Start by claiming your profile at business.google.com if you have not already. Fill in every field: your correct business name, your physical address in Iligan City, your service area if you cover nearby areas like Cagayan de Oro or Marawi, your phone number, website URL, business hours, and your primary category.</p>
        <p>The category you choose matters more than most owners realise. If you run a dental clinic, "Dentist" places you ahead of "Healthcare" for searches specific to dental services. Choose the most precise primary category Google offers, then add secondary categories where they genuinely apply.</p>
        <p>After the basics, add photos. Upload images of your premises, your team, and your work. Real, current photos outperform stock images every time. Finally, respond to every review — Google treats active, engaged profiles as more legitimate than dormant ones.</p>
        <h2>On-page signals that place you in Iligan searches</h2>
        <p>Your Google Business Profile gets you into Maps results. Your website handles the organic search results below it. Both work together; neither replaces the other.</p>
        <p>For local SEO in Iligan to work, Google needs to see clear location signals on your site. That means your address — Iligan City, Lanao del Norte, Philippines — appears on your Contact page and in your footer. Your page copy should mention the city and region naturally, as part of how you describe who you serve, not crammed in for its own sake. If you would rather have it done for you, see our <a href="https://www.fazeddigital.com/web-design-iligan-city">web design and local SEO service in Iligan City</a>.</p>
        <p>If you serve specific areas or nearby towns, a dedicated page per location works well for larger service businesses. A cleaning company that operates across Iligan and Cagayan de Oro can create a short, genuine page for each rather than competing for all of them on a single homepage.</p>
        <p>Your page titles and meta descriptions should include both your service and your city. "Dental Clinic in Iligan City — Book an Appointment" targets the search better than "Welcome to Our Clinic." <strong>Clarity works better than cleverness here.</strong> Schema markup (structured data) further tells Google your name, address, and category in a format it reads directly — a developer can add LocalBusiness schema to your site in under an hour.</p>
        <p>For a broader look at the signals that affect local rankings, our post on <a href="https://www.fazeddigital.com/blog/local-seo-small-business-guide">local SEO for small businesses</a> covers the full framework.</p>
        <h2>Getting citations right for Iligan businesses</h2>
        <p>A citation is any mention of your business name, address, and phone number on another website. Philippine business directories, industry listings, and local news sites all count. The value of citations is not the traffic they send — it is the consistency signal they give Google. When the same name, address, and number appear across multiple sites, Google treats your location as confirmed.</p>
        <p>Check any directories where you are already listed. Inconsistencies — a street name spelled two ways, an old phone number — dilute the signal. Fix them so every listing matches your Google Business Profile exactly.</p>
        <p>For Iligan-based businesses, list your business consistently on reputable Philippine directories and on any industry associations with online directories. Use exactly the same name, address and phone number everywhere. Local chambers of commerce listings also carry weight for searches specific to Northern Mindanao.</p>
        <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
        <p><strong>How long does local SEO in Iligan City take to show results?</strong> For Google Business Profile improvements, you can see movement within a few weeks of completing your profile and gathering recent reviews. On-page changes to your website typically take one to three months to reflect in organic rankings, depending on how often Google crawls your site.</p>
        <p><strong>Do I need a website if I already have a Google Business Profile?</strong> A profile alone helps you appear in Maps. A website gives you a second channel in organic search results and a place to explain your services, show your work, and capture enquiries. Most local businesses that rank consistently in Iligan have both.</p>
        <p><strong>How competitive is SEO in Iligan versus other Mindanao cities?</strong> In our experience, Iligan searches usually have fewer competing businesses than Cagayan de Oro, a larger city, so a business that covers the basics can often reach the top of local results sooner.</p>
        <p>If you want your Iligan City business to appear consistently in local search, our team can handle the technical and content work for you. See what is included at our <a href="https://www.fazeddigital.com/services#seo">SEO services page</a>.</p>
      `,
