        <h2>Why US businesses outsource web development to the Philippines</h2>
        <p>The Philippine web industry has grown into a credible option for US small businesses. Rates vary widely from studio to studio, and many Philippine agencies list their hourly rates and minimum project sizes on directories such as GoodFirms and DesignRush, which makes quotes easy to compare. The quality gap that existed ten years ago has largely closed: Filipino developers and designers work across the same tools and follow the same web standards as their US counterparts.</p>
        <p>There are two main reasons US owners choose to outsource: budget and turnaround. A fixed-price studio can build a complete website in 7–10 business days if the content is ready, compared to the weeks a larger agency might take while managing many simultaneous projects. A Philippine studio that specializes in small business sites will often outperform a generalist freelancer at a similar price point.</p>
