        <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
        <p><strong>Is it safe to outsource web development to the Philippines?</strong> Yes, provided you work with a studio that has a verifiable portfolio, clear ownership terms, and a fixed-price contract. The risk is not the location — it is working without a written agreement or with a team that cannot show finished work.</p>
        <p><strong>How do we collaborate across completely different time zones?</strong> Most studios send you a staging link to review at your own pace. You send written feedback, they apply changes during their working day, and you review again. Scheduled calls happen during the overlap window: early morning US Eastern or Pacific time.</p>
        <p><strong>Can I get ongoing support after the site launches?</strong> Reputable studios offer care plans that cover updates, backups, and support for a monthly fee — typically from $99 per month. These are optional: you are not required to stay on a retainer to keep your site running.</p>
        <p>To see what is included in a fixed-price build, <a href="https://www.fazeddigital.com/lp/7-day-website">browse our 7-day website package</a> — packages, prices, and how to reserve a spot.</p>
